# Server-to-server calls: keep the application API key in the Tariff backend.
# Tariff must verify its logged-in user's session ownership before create/revoke.
# The Tariff share page calls its public proxy; these core routes require the same key.
# New shareToken values are 36-character UUIDv4 strings, separate from session IDs.
# Previously created 43-character tokens remain valid for reading and revocation.
# Forward either token unchanged to the core routes; do not truncate or replace it.
@core = https://dev-customs-regulations.singlewindow.io
@apiKey = REPLACE_WITH_APPLICATION_API_KEY
@sessionId = REPLACE_WITH_OWNED_SESSION_UUID
@shareToken = REPLACE_WITH_CREATE_RESPONSE_TOKEN

### Create a live link. A missing body uses https://tariff.singlewindow.io/chat/shared.
POST {{core}}/api/chat/chat-session/{{sessionId}}/share
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"share_url_base":"https://tariff.singlewindow.io/chat/shared"}

### Read current messages. Repeat after sending another message to the same session.
GET {{core}}/api/chat/shared/{{shareToken}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Revoke this link. Further reads return 404; deleting the session also closes links.
DELETE {{core}}/api/chat/shared/{{shareToken}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

# Tariff proxy route: GET /api/v1-0/chat/shared/{shareToken}/messages.
# Forward the token to the core GET above and return its JSON with no-store caching.
# Render response.messages in order; session contains title, dates and visible count.
# New messages appear on the next GET. Polling or refresh is needed on an open page.
# The selected conversation branch is shown. Unfinished/error/private internal data is omitted.
# Citations contain number/title and optional public URL; core file previews are not exposed.
# A response shareUrl is a Tariff URL. Tariff must connect its page/proxy to these core routes.
